# Line endings, added 2026-08-09.
#
# Without this file, Git for Windows checks out with core.autocrlf=true and rewrites every LF to
# CRLF in the working tree. Prettier is configured with "endOfLine": "lf", so it then reports all
# 76 text files as badly formatted and `npm run verify` fails on a clean clone. Nothing is actually
# wrong with the content: every newline in the affected files is a CRLF pair, and the same files
# pass with --end-of-line auto.
#
# CI could never catch this. It runs on ubuntu-latest, which performs no conversion, so the
# pipeline is structurally blind to it while docs/LOCAL-SETUP.md promises a green verify on Windows.
#
# eol=lf makes the working tree match the repository on every platform, which is what Prettier,
# ESLint and the Vite build all already assume.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, so never touched by the above.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.zip binary
